# Components, Tailwind & Motion

## Structure

- `components/` — site personality and layout (Hero, cards, header/footer).
- `components/ui/` — small domain-independent primitives used across pages (Button, etc.).
- `components/mdx/` — MDX-only renderers.
- `components/motion/` — cursor, celestial background, theme toggle, motion utilities.
- One component per file; file name matches the export (`ProjectCard.tsx` → `ProjectCard`).

## Typography

- **Display / headings:** Space Grotesk via `next/font` → CSS var `--font-display` / Tailwind `font-display` (matches Lovable reference).
- **Body / UI:** DM Sans via `next/font` → CSS var `--font-sans` / Tailwind `font-sans`.
- Do not reintroduce Fraunces, Inter, Roboto, or generic system stacks as primary type.

## Tailwind

- Utility-first; extract repeated class strings with `cn()` (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) in `lib/cn.ts`.
- Design tokens via CSS variables in `app/globals.css` + Tailwind theme extension — not hard-coded ad-hoc hex scattered in JSX.
- No inline `style=` except for true dynamic values (e.g. motion transforms, clip-path origin).
- Mobile-first responsive utilities (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).

## Accessibility

- Semantic landmarks: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `footer`.
- Interactive elements are real buttons/links — not clickable `div`s.
- Visible focus rings; do not remove outline without a replacement.
- Images require meaningful `alt` (or empty alt when decorative).

## Motion (Framer Motion)

- Only library: Framer Motion (no GSAP, no extra cursor packages).
- Gate desktop-only effects with `(pointer: fine)`.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: skip or instant-apply transitions.
- Prefer `transform` and `opacity`; avoid animating layout-triggering properties.

## Forms

- Every control needs a label (visible or `aria-label`).
- Client validation is UX only; server validation is authoritative.
